0,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Thulung,Sino-Tibetan
1,Thulung language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thulung_language,"January 1, 2026 - Thulung or Thulung lwa (थुलुङ ल्वा) is a Sino-Tibetan Kirati languages or Thulung language spoken in parts of Nepal and Sikkim.",Thulung,Sino-Tibetan
2,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"May 6, 2025 - You will find that flutes and lutes combine with some percussion beats to create a soft aroma of music that is thought to resemble a constant communication link with the divine world, one that only ""perfect beings"" are able to compose. It is officially named Sino-Mongolian music and is heard in the streets during festivals and parties.",Thulung,Sino-Tibetan
